main.cpp
--cpp20
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [temp.deduct]/8, [temp.constr]: the two-parameter function template
`add(T,U)` constrained by `requires requires(T a, U b){ a + b; }` should be
viable for `add(1, 2)` (int + int is valid), so the asserts should verify.  CBMC
instead drops `add` from the candidate set (a latent deduction/requires bug for a
multi-parameter requires-constrained function template), leaving the call with
no viable function.

This test previously passed only VACUOUSLY: `add` was silently dropped and the
call's failure swallowed, so the body was truncated and the asserts were never
checked (proven: replacing the assertion with a deliberately false one still
reported VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL).  The SFINAE-enforcement fix (diagnose an
unrecovered no-viable-function call) now surfaces the real failure as a
CONVERSION ERROR.  Flip back to CORE once `add` is resolved correctly.
